course: dictionary
lesson: 7642
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right. Program can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Read the clues before you choose.
explain: «Ella wants to program a robot to dance.» Here program is a verb, so it means to write the instructions that tell the robot what to do. Try the swap: "Ella wants to write instructions for a robot to dance." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The same program runs many copies at once, each one answering a different person.» Here program is a noun. It is the set of instructions itself. The word "runs" is a clue, because you run a program on a computer, not a show.
explain: Americans also use program for a TV show, as in «a TV program». When you read something from another place, check the clues around the word. If you are still unsure, look it up in a dictionary.
fact: A program is a set of instructions that tells a computer what to do.
fact: To program means to write these instructions, so «program a robot» means to give a robot its instructions.
fact: In American English, a program can also be a TV or radio show, or a plan of activities, such as an «after-school program».
fact: Phrases like «computer program» and «program a robot» are common in computing lessons.
fact: «Known issue» means a bug, which is a mistake in a computer program that has not been fixed.
exercise: «A computer does not feel, want or know anything; it only follows its programs.» What is a program in this sentence? | Something you switch on at night | *A set of instructions that tells a computer what to do | A kind of cable | A picture drawn by a child
exercise: Ben says, «I want to program a robot to dance.» What does program mean here? | To wash a robot | To watch a robot on TV | *To write the instructions that tell a robot what to do | To turn a robot into a computer
exercise: «Early programs were not typed on screens: people punched holes into cards.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the holes were made. | *punched | typed | early | screens
test: «A known issue means a bug that has not been fixed.» What is a bug in this sentence? | A small insect that lives in gardens | A type of computer cable | A kind of screen | *A mistake in a computer program that has not been fixed
test: What does program mean in «Mia will program a game using code»? | Sell the game at a shop | Draw pictures for the game | *Write the instructions using code | Watch closely
exam: Which sentence uses program as a noun? | Let's program the robot now. | Dad will program the video recorder. | We will program the games tomorrow. | *The computer program sorts all the photos.
